  "body": "Reported by the maintainer in chat, 2026-11-14:\n\n> bug; when selecting twwo edges and clicking 2D generate on a 2D operation i get the error \"generate failed: could not generate the toolpath: 2D Offset1: invalid machining parameters: edge chain 0x148aab7f74e64a39 of 'Block-w-slot' is an open run - a 2D Offset cannot end mid-edge; select a closed chain - Ctrl+click the remaining edges, or Shift+click to take the whole loop\" - this should not be the case. It should generate path up to the edge of the stock.. And the Extend past - should extend that reach outside of the stock in the direction of the edges..\n\nWhat happens:\n- The geometry selection of a 2D Offset holds two open edges of the model `Block-w-slot`.\n- Generate refuses the operation with the message above.\n\nWhat must happen:\n- Two open edges are the walls of a region with open ends.\n- The operation cuts the region between the two edges. The open ends reach to the edge of the stock.\n- The parameter \"Extend past\" moves each open end out of the stock, in the direction of the edges.\n- The tool does not go around the corner at the end of an edge.\n\nEvidence:\n- `crates/app/src/operation/selection.rs` (`selection_geometry_in`): the Pocket family, Trace and Engrave refuse an open edge run. See the worker's finding in issue 1726 (https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/1726#issuecomment-6885264345).\n- Issue 1726 now tracks only the pick defect (the first Ctrl+click does not add the second edge). This issue tracks the toolpath.\n\nSafety:\n- The two edges are walls. The gouge check must judge the new moves against the model. A cut into the part must block the post.\n- A selection that does not give a clear region (edges that are not opposite, one edge only, edges at different heights) must be refused with a message that names the cause.\n\nDone means:\n- A 2D Offset, a 2D Pocket and a 2D Adaptive with two opposite open edges generate a toolpath between the edges, up to the stock edge.\n- \"Extend past\" moves the open ends out of the stock, and a test pins the distance.\n- A test shows that the tool does not cut past a wall edge.\n- A test shows that an unclear selection is refused by name.\n",
